<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#tyrian-purple">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tyrian purple</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as purple-dyed, murex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tyrian purple is a deep purple dye produced from murex sea snails, named after the Phoenician city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a>. Its production required huge numbers of shellfish, making it extremely costly and a symbol of royalty and high status. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a> treat purple-dyed textiles as a valuable product of Phoenician and Carthaginian commerce.</p></div>
